WEBVTT

00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:19.110
I see you didn't go to Shiga- <i>san</i> 's funeral.

00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:20.530
Yes.

00:00:20.530 --> 00:00:22.610
Can I ask why?

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:28.610
I already went to his funeral once.
That was enough.

00:00:28.610 --> 00:00:29.860
I see.

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:36.780
And for some reason, it doesn't feel
to me like he's really gone.

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:45.690
It's like he's right next to me,
like he's talking to me if I open his book...

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:50.820
He may still be with us,
even if his soul shatters.

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:55.690
Yes. As long as the books he spent
his life creating are still there.

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:58.450
"No Longer Human"

00:01:01.730 --> 00:01:02.980
Sorry to bother you.

00:01:02.980 --> 00:01:04.070
See you later.

00:01:04.070 --> 00:01:06.320
No, thank you.

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:53.440
"Episode 8"

00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:53.570
A fan club?

00:02:53.570 --> 00:02:59.320
Yes. I want to start a fan club
to cheer up Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> .

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:00.860
Great idea, huh?

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:06.320
Yeah, he's been a little down
since what happened with Shiga- <i>san</i> .

00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:07.440
I can understand why, though.

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:12.110
And when I see him, it makes my heart ache!

00:03:12.110 --> 00:03:14.480
I want him to cheer up...

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:19.070
I get that, but why come to us?

00:03:19.070 --> 00:03:23.190
There was once a club to try
and cheer up Shusei- <i>san</i> , right?

00:03:23.190 --> 00:03:29.030
Yeah, I remember that! The Shusei Fan Club!

00:03:29.030 --> 00:03:33.530
Sai talked to a bunch of authors
to get it together, right?

00:03:33.530 --> 00:03:37.110
They wanted to help out
Shusei- <i>san</i> --he was in a slump.

00:03:37.110 --> 00:03:39.690
Don't say slump. It's rude.

00:03:40.610 --> 00:03:41.860
You were totally in a slump.

00:03:41.860 --> 00:03:44.440
You went and learned to dance instead.

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:45.780
Hey, Saisei- <i>san</i> .

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:47.480
Dancing?

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:50.030
It was hilarious.

00:03:50.030 --> 00:03:52.820
I just didn't know what to do.

00:03:52.820 --> 00:03:54.360
You were in a slump.

00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:56.900
I was not in a slump.
I was just having a rough patch!

00:03:56.900 --> 00:03:59.360
Anybody who saw that dance
would think to themselves

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:02.320
that you were headed for a bad end.

00:04:02.320 --> 00:04:05.150
So we wanted to help him out.

00:04:05.150 --> 00:04:07.860
And you made the Shusei Fan Club?

00:04:07.860 --> 00:04:08.900
Yup.

00:04:08.900 --> 00:04:14.980
But it was Shimazaki- <i>san</i> who started
the club to support Tokuda Shusei.

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:17.280
Why not ask him?

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:18.780
That's impossible.

00:04:18.780 --> 00:04:19.940
Impossible, yeah.

00:04:21.070 --> 00:04:22.440
Yeah.

00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:27.150
I think he'd be the best person to ask, too.

00:04:27.150 --> 00:04:30.150
Why don't they get along?

00:04:30.150 --> 00:04:35.690
I don't think it's that they don't get along.

00:04:36.780 --> 00:04:40.780
Why don't you tell me a story?

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:43.360
My stories are dull.

00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:44.940
I'm aware.

00:04:44.940 --> 00:04:47.980
It's not whether it's interesting or dull.

00:04:47.980 --> 00:04:50.230
It's whether it's interesting or not.

00:04:50.230 --> 00:04:52.570
I don't find you interesting at all.

00:04:52.570 --> 00:04:54.440
I'm aware.

00:04:54.440 --> 00:04:56.730
But that doesn't matter.

00:04:56.730 --> 00:04:59.530
I'm not the one talking.

00:04:59.530 --> 00:05:02.190
You're very heavy-handed.

00:05:02.190 --> 00:05:04.690
Just like your books.

00:05:08.690 --> 00:05:09.940
Are you mad?

00:05:09.940 --> 00:05:11.320
No.

00:05:11.320 --> 00:05:14.690
Just confused because I don't understand.

00:05:14.690 --> 00:05:15.690
Really?

00:05:15.690 --> 00:05:16.980
Really.

00:05:16.980 --> 00:05:19.030
How long are you going to follow me?

00:05:19.030 --> 00:05:20.780
Until you talk.

00:05:20.780 --> 00:05:23.320
No. I don't want to talk.

00:05:23.320 --> 00:05:26.940
Well, I say no to your no.
I want to hear your story.

00:05:26.940 --> 00:05:28.570
You're persistent.

00:05:28.570 --> 00:05:30.070
You just figured that out?

00:05:30.070 --> 00:05:31.690
I have nothing to say.

00:05:31.690 --> 00:05:33.980
I have questions to ask.

00:05:42.570 --> 00:05:43.570
What?

00:05:48.150 --> 00:05:49.940
No running in the hall!

00:05:52.190 --> 00:05:53.860
What's going on?

00:05:53.860 --> 00:05:55.150
Sorry.

00:05:55.150 --> 00:05:57.360
Can I have something to drink?

00:05:57.360 --> 00:05:58.690
Wait!

00:05:59.570 --> 00:06:01.360
What's this?

00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:05.860
Ango-broth, from my special ango-soup.

00:06:05.860 --> 00:06:08.730
Well? Tastes like corruption, right?

00:06:09.730 --> 00:06:11.940
Incredible...

00:06:11.940 --> 00:06:14.320
What did I just say?

00:06:14.320 --> 00:06:19.150
Even the great Akutagawa Ryunosuke
does not understand the taste of corruption?

00:06:19.150 --> 00:06:20.360
A shame.

00:06:20.360 --> 00:06:24.150
Taste of corruption aside,
I'm glad I found you.

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:26.730
I had a question for you.

00:06:26.730 --> 00:06:28.190
For us?

00:06:29.440 --> 00:06:32.360
About Dazai?

00:06:32.360 --> 00:06:37.150
I can tell you all you want about Dazai.

00:06:37.150 --> 00:06:39.360
Most of it will be bad.

00:06:39.360 --> 00:06:41.360
Really?

00:06:41.360 --> 00:06:43.610
He's not a bad guy,

00:06:43.610 --> 00:06:46.480
but he is a loser.

00:06:46.480 --> 00:06:52.360
If he wasn't, he wouldn't have
attempted suicide so many times.

00:06:52.360 --> 00:06:59.230
Dazai was... well, he was
trying his best to cope.

00:06:59.230 --> 00:07:00.820
Cope?

00:07:00.820 --> 00:07:06.980
I think he lacked the skills
to get by in the real world.

00:07:06.980 --> 00:07:11.190
Most people, when that happens,
just turn into madmen.

00:07:11.190 --> 00:07:13.030
But he refused.

00:07:13.030 --> 00:07:16.150
He always tried to be human.

00:07:16.150 --> 00:07:20.610
If only he'd fallen and been corrupted,
it would've been easier for him.

00:07:20.610 --> 00:07:22.440
But he didn't.

00:07:22.440 --> 00:07:24.900
He's a deeply sincere man, in the end.

00:07:24.900 --> 00:07:31.030
The one closest to him
in the end may have been Dan- <i>kun</i> .

00:07:31.030 --> 00:07:32.230
Dan?

00:07:32.230 --> 00:07:34.780
Dan. Dan Kazuo.

00:07:34.780 --> 00:07:37.860
Another one of our group.

00:07:37.860 --> 00:07:42.190
But he tried to understand him
more than anything.

00:07:42.190 --> 00:07:45.320
They once almost committed suicide together.

00:07:45.320 --> 00:07:47.030
Normally you couldn't do that.

00:07:47.030 --> 00:07:48.570
And that's not all.

00:07:48.570 --> 00:07:53.230
After Dazai's death, he wrote a book
called <i>Dazai Osamu: The Novel</i> .

00:07:53.230 --> 00:07:56.440
That goes beyond "understanding"
and turns him into a mere fan.

00:07:56.440 --> 00:07:58.110
Dan Kazuo.

00:07:58.110 --> 00:08:04.400
Even with someone who understood him
so well, he still chose death, right?

00:08:04.400 --> 00:08:06.690
Yup.

00:08:06.690 --> 00:08:08.610
What are you doing?

00:08:08.610 --> 00:08:09.980
Why?

00:08:09.980 --> 00:08:12.280
Tobacco. Looks great, right?

00:08:12.280 --> 00:08:13.480
Tobacco?

00:08:13.480 --> 00:08:17.650
We tried to figure out what
Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> would like.

00:08:17.650 --> 00:08:19.610
And it's tobacco, right?

00:08:19.610 --> 00:08:23.690
He'd love it if we gave him
a lifetime supply, right?

00:08:23.690 --> 00:08:29.110
It's the perfect activity for
the Akutagawa Fan Club!

00:08:29.110 --> 00:08:30.530
Fools!

00:08:30.530 --> 00:08:35.530
How could you grow
such a dangerous plant in this holy library?

00:08:35.530 --> 00:08:38.360
That's a terrible thing to say!

00:08:38.360 --> 00:08:43.320
Tobacco has never been made illegal in Japan!

00:08:43.320 --> 00:08:45.360
That's not the issue!

00:08:45.360 --> 00:08:49.110
What, would you have preferred
we plant a tuna farm?

00:08:49.110 --> 00:08:51.110
A tuna farm would be fine.

00:08:51.110 --> 00:08:52.280
It would be?

00:08:52.280 --> 00:08:55.320
You can't plant tuna, Sai.

00:08:55.320 --> 00:08:58.570
It's an example.

00:08:58.570 --> 00:09:03.320
Anyway, no growing addictive
substances in the library!

00:09:03.320 --> 00:09:05.480
Is that a rule?

00:09:05.480 --> 00:09:06.900
I just made it a rule!

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:08.320
No fair!

00:09:08.320 --> 00:09:10.610
Give authors their freedom!

00:09:10.610 --> 00:09:16.070
I think Dazai- <i>kun</i> is
a nicer man than anyone else.

00:09:16.070 --> 00:09:19.230
So he tries to make people
happier more than anybody.

00:09:19.230 --> 00:09:21.900
And sometimes he goes too far.

00:09:24.360 --> 00:09:26.150
What are you doing?

00:09:26.150 --> 00:09:28.400
Huh? It's not allowed, right?

00:09:28.400 --> 00:09:30.730
So we have to get rid of the tobacco.

00:09:30.730 --> 00:09:33.190
Don't tell me...

00:09:33.190 --> 00:09:35.440
This is the fastest way, right?

00:09:38.780 --> 00:09:40.690
Crap! Water!

00:09:43.440 --> 00:09:44.610
A clown?

00:09:44.610 --> 00:09:50.610
Yeah. At his core, he doesn't
understand how people think.

00:09:50.610 --> 00:09:54.400
But he wants them to be happy.

00:09:54.400 --> 00:09:56.230
Dazai- <i>kun</i> !

00:09:56.230 --> 00:09:58.980
And so he has to pretend to be a clown.

00:10:00.940 --> 00:10:07.730
Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> ,
I brought you a lot of tobacco!

00:10:07.730 --> 00:10:12.320
I couldn't last with
that lifestyle for a second.

00:10:12.320 --> 00:10:16.030
So I thought he lasted a pretty long time.

00:10:16.030 --> 00:10:21.190
He lacks what makes you human,
but tries to be human more than anyone else.

00:10:21.190 --> 00:10:25.190
If you want to know about him,
you can find out right there.

00:10:25.190 --> 00:10:28.940
"No Longer Human"

00:10:25.190 --> 00:10:28.940
If you read that, you'll figure out who he is.

00:10:30.280 --> 00:10:32.570
I see. You're right.

00:10:32.570 --> 00:10:36.570
If you want to know about an author,
the thing to do is read their books.

00:10:36.570 --> 00:10:38.110
That's normal.

00:10:38.110 --> 00:10:43.150
To be honest, I was a bit uncertain myself.

00:10:43.150 --> 00:10:47.150
I wasn't sure if I should touch
the most well-known work

00:10:47.150 --> 00:10:49.440
of the man who respects me so much.

00:10:49.440 --> 00:10:53.030
But you've helped me decide.

00:10:53.030 --> 00:10:54.610
Thank you.

00:11:03.030 --> 00:11:04.530
I'm reading.

00:11:04.530 --> 00:11:06.610
I can tell.

00:11:06.610 --> 00:11:12.230
Is it very rare for you to be
so interested in another?

00:11:13.940 --> 00:11:17.860
Akutagawa Ryunosuke is a rare sort of author,

00:11:17.860 --> 00:11:22.940
one who completely denied
his later works in his early years.

00:11:22.940 --> 00:11:24.980
I can't understand that.

00:11:24.980 --> 00:11:26.400
You think so?

00:11:26.400 --> 00:11:28.980
I don't think it's that rare.

00:11:28.980 --> 00:11:31.900
Men change.

00:11:31.900 --> 00:11:34.900
The core of a man never changes.

00:11:34.900 --> 00:11:37.070
That's why it's so strange.

00:11:37.070 --> 00:11:39.230
What are you trying to say?

00:11:39.230 --> 00:11:43.480
Authors are tricky creatures.

00:11:43.480 --> 00:11:46.860
Their writing style is decided, to a degree,

00:11:46.860 --> 00:11:49.190
by their environment
and the lives they've lived.

00:11:49.190 --> 00:11:52.400
It's not something they can change.

00:11:52.400 --> 00:11:54.610
But that's normal.

00:11:56.110 --> 00:12:00.230
Your works were well-respected.

00:12:00.230 --> 00:12:03.780
<i>Rashomon. The Spider's Thread. Portrait of Hell.</i>

00:12:03.780 --> 00:12:11.650
"Rashomon" "Portrait of Hell" "Spider's Thread"

00:12:04.650 --> 00:12:11.650
All of them are famous for their ability
to entice the reader's attention.

00:12:12.070 --> 00:12:18.440
And these works are the core of
the author named Akutagawa Ryunosuke.

00:12:18.440 --> 00:12:21.400
You think so, do you?

00:12:21.400 --> 00:12:23.690
That wasn't my opinion.

00:12:23.690 --> 00:12:25.860
It's the opinion of the masses.

00:12:25.860 --> 00:12:29.190
The latter half seemed to be
your own original nonsense.

00:12:29.190 --> 00:12:31.980
Oh, you noticed?

00:12:31.980 --> 00:12:34.070
I made a hypothesis, that's all.

00:12:34.070 --> 00:12:36.400
You seem insistent on bothering me,

00:12:36.400 --> 00:12:40.280
so I'll go back to my room to read.

00:12:40.280 --> 00:12:44.280
The early Akutagawa,
who entranced readers with his stories,

00:12:44.280 --> 00:12:47.650
and the later Akutagawa,
who rejected that style,

00:12:47.650 --> 00:12:49.820
were different people.

00:12:51.780 --> 00:12:57.440
In your later years, your work
was of a clearly different color.

00:12:57.440 --> 00:13:01.400
<i>The Mirage. Kappa. Gears.</i>

00:13:01.400 --> 00:13:06.860
All of them famous,
but far from your true style.

00:13:06.860 --> 00:13:12.400
It would make more sense to me
if a totally different person wrote them.

00:13:14.110 --> 00:13:16.320
An interesting theory.

00:13:16.320 --> 00:13:21.610
So does that mean there were
two Akutagawa Ryunosukes?

00:13:21.610 --> 00:13:26.070
It's hard to imagine a different
person impersonating you.

00:13:26.070 --> 00:13:30.980
So I came up with a different idea.

00:13:30.980 --> 00:13:39.070
Perhaps the later works were written by
a Taint within Akutagawa Ryunosuke.

00:13:40.360 --> 00:13:43.650
The Taints are, given what we know,

00:13:43.650 --> 00:13:51.610
likely a collection of negative feelings
towards literature, I believe.

00:13:51.610 --> 00:13:55.860
But in fact, there's much we don't know.

00:13:56.940 --> 00:13:59.650
Let's say that negative hatreds
towards Akutagawa Ryunosuke,

00:13:59.650 --> 00:14:04.230
the Japanese novelist, gathered in one place.

00:14:04.230 --> 00:14:14.400
Those hatreds would be angry and jealous
of your early works. They'd despise them.

00:14:14.400 --> 00:14:18.440
They'd do anything to stop you
from creating more.

00:14:18.440 --> 00:14:21.980
So they'd possess me, take over my body,

00:14:21.980 --> 00:14:26.150
and force me to write new works
that denied my earlier ones?

00:14:26.150 --> 00:14:28.150
Is that your theory?

00:14:28.150 --> 00:14:30.530
Don't you find it fascinating?

00:14:30.530 --> 00:14:31.610
No.

00:14:31.610 --> 00:14:33.690
Of course, I do have my doubts.

00:14:33.690 --> 00:14:38.280
Can a Taint even write a book?

00:14:38.280 --> 00:14:43.690
But if they could,
wouldn't that be a huge discovery?

00:14:43.690 --> 00:14:51.570
So you're trying to say that the later
Akutagawa Ryunosuke was a taint.

00:14:51.570 --> 00:14:55.150
What would that make you, if that were true?

00:14:56.400 --> 00:15:00.230
Would half of you be a Taint?

00:15:03.110 --> 00:15:08.110
All this and more in Shimazaki Toson's
shocking new novel.

00:15:08.110 --> 00:15:12.570
It would make for a fun plot.

00:15:12.570 --> 00:15:13.730
I see.

00:15:13.730 --> 00:15:16.440
I hadn't thought of that.

00:15:16.440 --> 00:15:19.280
I was right to begin with.

00:15:19.280 --> 00:15:21.320
I've nothing to say to you.

00:15:21.320 --> 00:15:22.730
I see.

00:15:30.280 --> 00:15:33.440
You said that to Akutagawa- <i>san</i> ?

00:15:33.440 --> 00:15:34.780
That's crazy.

00:15:34.780 --> 00:15:37.440
Yes. It is.

00:15:37.440 --> 00:15:42.900
The works of the later Akutagawa Ryunosuke
were written by a Taint.

00:15:42.900 --> 00:15:47.480
I understand myself that this is impossible.

00:15:48.820 --> 00:15:50.690
But...

00:15:50.690 --> 00:15:54.530
It's the only thing that seems true to me.

00:15:55.530 --> 00:15:59.780
You knew about my family, right?

00:15:59.780 --> 00:16:01.730
Yes.

00:16:01.730 --> 00:16:04.360
My father never fit into society.

00:16:04.360 --> 00:16:08.860
He continued to rebel against it
no matter how much he suffered.

00:16:08.860 --> 00:16:12.610
And then he died in jail.

00:16:12.610 --> 00:16:17.400
Afterwards, my mother
and older sister died of illness.

00:16:17.400 --> 00:16:22.440
And my eldest brother was thrown in jail.

00:16:22.440 --> 00:16:28.860
My father's actions changed our family's fate.

00:16:28.860 --> 00:16:31.780
That's not an appropriate mealtime topic.

00:16:31.780 --> 00:16:34.780
I've never hated my father.

00:16:34.780 --> 00:16:39.360
But because of that experience, I think...

00:16:39.360 --> 00:16:42.480
People can't change that easy.

00:16:42.480 --> 00:16:47.190
If they could, my father wouldn't
have needed to commit suicide.

00:16:47.190 --> 00:16:48.940
Shimazaki...

00:16:48.940 --> 00:16:54.110
In the end, I just want
an answer I can accept, is all.

00:16:54.110 --> 00:16:59.360
Akutagawa Ryunosuke denied
his earlier works and changed.

00:16:59.360 --> 00:17:02.150
I can't understand him.

00:17:02.150 --> 00:17:07.440
It would make more sense if
something else had taken him over.

00:17:07.440 --> 00:17:12.730
And that's the reason you've been
going after him for so long?

00:17:12.730 --> 00:17:14.150
I don't know.

00:17:14.150 --> 00:17:16.780
If there was another reason...

00:17:16.780 --> 00:17:21.070
It's that I don't think an author
should ever deny their own style.

00:17:21.070 --> 00:17:24.860
Their style, or their view of the world...

00:17:24.860 --> 00:17:27.570
You've never denied yours?

00:17:27.570 --> 00:17:28.690
No.

00:17:28.690 --> 00:17:32.940
I recognize that I'm unhappy.

00:17:32.940 --> 00:17:40.280
But that unhappiness was needed
for me to be the author I am.

00:17:40.280 --> 00:17:45.570
So this world, which I've crafted
by overcoming my family's death,

00:17:45.570 --> 00:17:48.650
is not something I could deny.

00:17:48.650 --> 00:17:50.070
Listen, Shimazaki.

00:17:50.070 --> 00:17:53.530
I was barely able to remain an author because

00:17:53.530 --> 00:17:56.190
you made that fan club to support me.

00:17:56.190 --> 00:17:57.940
I still think that.

00:17:57.940 --> 00:18:01.070
Don't go thanking me now.

00:18:01.070 --> 00:18:02.650
It's creepy.

00:18:02.650 --> 00:18:04.230
That's not it.

00:18:04.230 --> 00:18:09.780
What I want to say is that without you,
I would've changed.

00:18:09.780 --> 00:18:14.280
Not everyone can constantly
remain true to themselves.

00:18:16.730 --> 00:18:19.230
The Akutagawa Fan Club, huh?

00:18:19.230 --> 00:18:20.440
That's right.

00:18:20.440 --> 00:18:24.820
I tried to give him tobacco as a present
as part of our activities.

00:18:24.820 --> 00:18:28.570
Jeez! I'm so mad at that cat!

00:18:28.570 --> 00:18:31.780
Yelling at a cat won't help you.

00:18:31.780 --> 00:18:35.480
Yeah. That cat's got it more
together than we do.

00:18:35.480 --> 00:18:38.570
Huh? Cats are animals.

00:18:38.570 --> 00:18:40.150
Yeah, but that's not saying much.

00:18:40.150 --> 00:18:42.070
Well, maybe not, but...

00:18:42.070 --> 00:18:43.570
There you are.

00:18:43.570 --> 00:18:45.480
Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> !

00:18:45.480 --> 00:18:48.570
I read your book.

00:18:49.650 --> 00:18:51.150
How did you like it?

00:18:51.150 --> 00:18:55.570
I don't like this book.

00:18:55.570 --> 00:18:57.480
<i>No Longer Human.</i>

00:18:57.480 --> 00:19:02.480
I find myself hating the mind
and driving motivations of its hero.

00:19:02.480 --> 00:19:04.230
I can't enjoy it at all.

00:19:04.230 --> 00:19:10.750
"No Longer Human"

00:19:04.230 --> 00:19:10.730
I can't understand why anyone
would consider it worth reading.

00:19:10.820 --> 00:19:12.110
But...

00:19:12.110 --> 00:19:19.730
I would also add that only the lowest
sort of man could've written it.

00:19:19.730 --> 00:19:24.030
A selfish psychopath causes
no end of trouble for other people,

00:19:24.030 --> 00:19:27.940
living life in a disgusting and shameful way.

00:19:29.360 --> 00:19:34.360
In a sense, it's well-written.

00:19:34.360 --> 00:19:37.230
As an excuse for a failure of a man.

00:19:37.230 --> 00:19:40.480
Hey, did you have to go that far?!

00:19:40.480 --> 00:19:43.570
You're joking, right, Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> ?

00:19:43.570 --> 00:19:47.940
You were always the person
I thought of when I wrote my books.

00:19:47.940 --> 00:19:49.110
So...

00:19:49.110 --> 00:19:52.230
You thought of me as you wrote this thing?

00:19:52.230 --> 00:19:54.360
That's not fair to me.

00:19:57.730 --> 00:19:58.650
Dazai?

00:19:58.650 --> 00:20:03.900
Begone from my sight
along with this worthless book.

00:20:10.230 --> 00:20:11.440
Dazai- <i>kun</i> !

00:20:11.440 --> 00:20:14.940
Dazai! Dazai! Wake up!

00:20:14.940 --> 00:20:17.690
Don't tell me...

00:20:17.820 --> 00:20:20.190
"No Longer Human"

00:20:25.780 --> 00:20:29.360
Why would I say such things?

00:20:32.030 --> 00:20:34.940
Akutagawa- <i>san</i> ? What happened?

00:20:37.190 --> 00:20:40.320
I'm sorry... but it seems...

00:20:41.360 --> 00:20:43.690
...you were right.

00:20:44.860 --> 00:20:46.440
Akutagawa- <i>san</i> !

00:20:49.440 --> 00:20:53.980
Sakaguchi and Oda were the
two that were called this time?

00:20:54.940 --> 00:20:58.440
Don't leave me out, peach-flower boy!

00:20:58.440 --> 00:21:00.820
You weren't part of the club.

00:21:00.820 --> 00:21:02.650
Where's Akutagawa- <i>san</i> ?

00:21:02.650 --> 00:21:06.940
Imprisoned for now, given the circumstances.

00:21:06.940 --> 00:21:12.480
I can't believe he was possessed by a Taint!

00:21:15.030 --> 00:21:17.440
Is that even possible?

00:21:17.440 --> 00:21:20.940
We don't know. But the priority now is Dazai.

00:21:20.940 --> 00:21:22.980
There's no time, guys.

00:21:22.980 --> 00:21:24.860
We know!

00:21:24.860 --> 00:21:27.150
We're coming for you, Dazai.

00:21:27.150 --> 00:21:29.860
We'll save you.

00:21:41.980 --> 00:21:43.730
I'm so bored.

00:21:48.230 --> 00:21:50.570
I hope they get here soon...

00:21:50.940 --> 00:21:53.940
"No Longer Human"

00:23:24.480 --> 00:23:25.900
Literary Gourmet!

00:23:24.750 --> 00:23:27.960
"Stop Being Plain Gorgeous Shiruko Chapter"

00:23:25.900 --> 00:23:29.650
Stop Being Plain Gorgeous Shiruko Chapter.

00:23:29.650 --> 00:23:33.360
Tokuda Shusei gets up very early in the morning.

00:23:33.360 --> 00:23:40.280
Lately, his favorite thing to do is liven up
his snack after his boring chores.

00:23:40.280 --> 00:23:43.030
He wants to stop being considered plain!

00:23:43.030 --> 00:23:46.440
So he at least wants his food to be fancy.

00:23:46.440 --> 00:23:50.570
So he carefully dusts it with gold flakes.

00:23:50.570 --> 00:23:54.530
Gold flakes have no flavor or taste
so they don't get in the way.

00:23:54.530 --> 00:23:57.650
It's got the perfect amount of
flavor and sweetness...

00:23:57.650 --> 00:23:59.780
It's plain, basically.

00:23:59.780 --> 00:24:00.780
Stop it!
